            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nNot at the moment, no.\r\n\r\n> I wanted to know if there are any plans on implementing project wide search and replace plugin in the mini lib.\r\n\r\nThe project wide search and replace I'd expect to be done slightly more traditional way:\r\n- Populate quickfix list with matches. For example, with `builtin.grep()`/`builtin.grep_live()` from 'mini.pick' after marking all matches (`<C-a>` by default) and converting them to quickfix list (`<M-CR>` by default).\r\n- Perform operations on quickfix list. Like with `:cdo`.\r\n\r\nThat said, I have vague plans to make working with quickfix/location lists easier. Not sure yet how though.\r\n\r\n> Also a diagnostics plugin like trouble.nvim combined with todo-comments.nvim.\r\n\r\nThe project wide diagnostics is better suited for Neovim core, in my opinion. The downside here is that I am not aware of the initiative to implement it yet, unfortunately.\r\n\r\nThe only thing from 'todo-comments.nvim' which I would like to support is highlighting which is already [implemented in 'mini.hipatterns'](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/c3b37f4afb933141a750b60b86fb6ef6b50d0e61/doc/mini-hipatterns.txt#L110-L124). Other than that, this looks similar to project wide find and replace functionality.\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned / planned in slightly different form.",
            "created_at": "2024-03-10T12:34:26Z",
