            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> edit: that was easy:\r\n> \r\n> ```lua\r\n>       mappings = {\r\n> \r\n>         to_quickfix = {\r\n>           char = \"<C-q>\",\r\n>           func = function()\r\n>             local items = MiniPick.get_picker_items() or {}\r\n>             MiniPick.default_choose_marked(items)\r\n>             MiniPick.stop()\r\n>           end,\r\n>         },\r\n>       },\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nI was going to mention that using `return true` instead of `MiniPick.stop()` should be a bit better, but realized that this was never documented (although tested). [It is now](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/a683bfe8e03293e3bb079e24c94e51977756a3ec/doc/mini-pick.txt#L592-L594). So thanks for the question and solution!",
